2046
01:34:34,108 --> 01:34:36,276
I saw the other posts.
Everyone's great at spinning a story.

2047
01:34:36,503 --> 01:34:38,137
- Everyone did pretty well.
- I couldn't pull it off.

2048
01:34:39,513 --> 01:34:41,931
I had no clue what to write
on the overseas soccer board.

2049
01:34:41,932 --> 01:34:42,949
I completely panicked.

2050
01:34:43,051 --> 01:34:44,417
Then I saw Benjamin's post.

2051
01:34:44,418 --> 01:34:45,718
It didn't fit...

2052
01:34:45,719 --> 01:34:48,054
- I know.
- his vibe at all.

2053
01:34:48,055 --> 01:34:50,423
- Seriously.
- He sounded like a longtime user.

2054
01:34:50,424 --> 01:34:51,324
For real.

2055
01:34:51,558 --> 01:34:52,791
He was using...

2056
01:34:52,792 --> 01:34:55,461
slang that even I didn't recognize.

2057
01:34:55,462 --> 01:34:57,663
How can you type like that
unless you're a native Korean speaker?

2058
01:34:57,664 --> 01:34:59,198
Those terms were legit board vernacular.

2059
01:34:59,700 --> 01:35:01,734
- You're out.
- I'm back.

2060
01:35:01,735 --> 01:35:04,571
Benjamin,
that caught me completely off guard.

2061
01:35:04,572 --> 01:35:05,905
You really shocked me.

2062
01:35:05,906 --> 01:35:08,541
You sounded like someone
who truly knows...

2063
01:35:08,542 --> 01:35:10,677
their way around online boards.

2064
01:35:12,613 --> 01:35:13,413
Is that so?

2065
01:35:17,351 --> 01:35:20,887
We will now announce the results
of the Covert Access Mission.

2066
01:35:22,222 --> 01:35:23,756
Round One results.

2067
01:35:24,201 --> 01:35:27,436
Benjamin...

2068
01:35:27,461 --> 01:35:29,629
took first place.

2069
01:35:29,630 --> 01:35:31,130
Benjamin is insane.

2070
01:35:32,800 --> 01:35:34,267
(2 upvotes)

2071
01:35:34,268 --> 01:35:35,769
(6 comments)

2072
01:35:36,970 --> 01:35:38,438
Round Two results.

2073
01:35:38,672 --> 01:35:40,406
Ted...

2074
01:35:40,407 --> 01:35:43,275
- Ted.
- took first place.

2075
01:35:43,477 --> 01:35:45,012
(16 upvotes)

2076
01:35:45,013 --> 01:35:46,479
(37 comments)

2077
01:35:47,114 --> 01:35:48,748
Round Three results.

2078
01:35:48,949 --> 01:35:51,551
Superman...

2079
01:35:51,552 --> 01:35:53,953
- took first place.
- He won!

2080
01:35:54,955 --> 01:35:56,489
(8 upvotes)

2081
01:35:56,490 --> 01:35:57,890
(15 comments)

2082
01:35:58,092 --> 01:36:01,093
Each of these three residents...

2083
01:36:01,094 --> 01:36:02,795
will receive 1,000 dollars.

2084
01:36:02,796 --> 01:36:05,264
(11,350 dollars, 6,820 dollars,
8,780 dollars)

2085
01:36:05,265 --> 01:36:07,099
(12,350 dollars, 7,820 dollars,
9,780 dollars)

2086
01:36:07,267 --> 01:36:08,099
I'm so jealous.

2087
01:36:09,136 --> 01:36:12,471
The resident with the lowest score
across all rounds is...

2088
01:36:17,244 --> 01:36:19,912
Sugar.

2089
01:36:25,151 --> 01:36:27,597
Today's eviction candidate
with the lowest combined mission...

2090
01:36:27,598 --> 01:36:28,820
and favorability score is...

2091
01:36:31,325 --> 01:36:33,993
Nangja.

2092
01:36:33,994 --> 01:36:36,596
Nangja.

2093
01:36:38,799 --> 01:36:40,833
I got way too careless.

2094
01:36:40,834 --> 01:36:44,438
I knew I was low on favorability votes...

2095
01:36:44,439 --> 01:36:46,339
from being the Reporter.

2096
01:36:46,506 --> 01:36:47,806
I even fell behind Banu.

2097
01:36:48,108 --> 01:36:48,736
Unbelievable.

2098
01:36:48,737 --> 01:36:50,142
(Nangja: right, equalism,
working-class, conservative)

2099
01:36:50,143 --> 01:36:51,610
Yesterday, Benjamin told me...

2100
01:36:51,611 --> 01:36:53,412
he'd vote for me every day...

2101
01:36:53,547 --> 01:36:55,614
and warned me to take
the favorability vote seriously.

2102
01:36:55,916 --> 01:36:58,918
The people who didn't step
on any toes racked up the votes.

2103
01:37:03,123 --> 01:37:07,793
Any resident who becomes
an eviction candidate will be evicted...

2104
01:37:08,028 --> 01:37:10,896
when the Community Center closes...

2105
01:37:11,331 --> 01:37:15,768
unless they submit an immunity card.

2106
01:37:18,972 --> 01:37:21,373
(Genie is the only one
holding an immunity card.)

2107
01:37:21,743 --> 01:37:23,042
We will now begin...

2108
01:37:23,210 --> 01:37:26,078
today's favorability vote.

2109
01:37:27,648 --> 01:37:32,218
The Community Center will close
in one hour.

2110
01:37:32,853 --> 01:37:35,855
(The favorability vote)

2111
01:37:38,692 --> 01:37:40,092
Ted, what did you post in Round Two?

2112
01:37:41,295 --> 01:37:43,195
- When I need a good cry...
- The movie one.

2113
01:37:43,196 --> 01:37:46,165
I asked what movies people watch
when they need to cry.

2114
01:37:46,633 --> 01:37:48,067
Everyone was so warm and supportive.

2115
01:37:48,068 --> 01:37:49,034
I know.

2116
01:37:50,671 --> 01:37:52,505
(The favorability vote)

2117
01:37:55,375 --> 01:37:56,542
First off,

2118
01:37:57,983 --> 01:38:00,451
we should run
the Reporter Information Check...

2119
01:38:00,614 --> 01:38:02,081
as soon as possible.

2120
01:38:04,051 --> 01:38:05,018
Put me to use.

2121
01:38:06,553 --> 01:38:07,420
They were just going to throw her away.

2122
01:38:07,421 --> 01:38:09,255
I couldn't stand seeing that.

2123
01:38:10,023 --> 01:38:12,524
One of the questions we brought up was...

2124
01:38:12,525 --> 01:38:14,594
"Among the residents..."

2125
01:38:14,595 --> 01:38:16,795
- "who has the most money?"
- "Who has the most money?"

2126
01:38:16,796 --> 01:38:18,364
"Who's sitting on the biggest prize pot?"

2127
01:38:18,365 --> 01:38:20,366
- Top three.
- Top three?

2128
01:38:20,367 --> 01:38:22,701
Since we can't be completely sure.

2129
01:38:23,203 --> 01:38:25,704
We don't know if the spy attempted
two eliminations.

2130
01:38:25,872 --> 01:38:27,739
- Two.
- Right.

2131
01:38:28,942 --> 01:38:31,544
Ask for the top three in rank order.

2132
01:38:31,545 --> 01:38:32,945
That should do it.

2133
01:38:32,946 --> 01:38:34,647
This will give us crucial intel...

2134
01:38:34,648 --> 01:38:37,516
because I know exactly
how much I had yesterday.

2135
01:38:37,517 --> 01:38:39,184
- Did it transfer over to them?
- I'm at zero dollars.

2136
01:38:39,185 --> 01:38:40,118
(The casualty's entire prize fund...)

2137
01:38:40,119 --> 01:38:41,086
(is transferred to the attacker.)

2138
01:38:41,087 --> 01:38:43,055
My prize money dropped to zero yesterday.

2139
01:38:43,757 --> 01:38:45,624
I was just brought back.

2140
01:38:47,361 --> 01:38:49,663
After the ten-percent tax,

2141
01:38:49,664 --> 01:38:51,097
I have 1,800 dollars left.

2142
01:38:51,098 --> 01:38:52,432
- The funds you received today.
- Yeah.

2143
01:38:53,033 --> 01:38:54,767
I'm penniless.

2144
01:38:55,335 --> 01:38:56,540
Completely broke.

2145
01:38:56,541 --> 01:38:57,536
(The favorability vote)

2146
01:38:58,072 --> 01:39:01,207
The second I realized I'd been targeted,
my balance was wiped clean.

2147
01:39:08,348 --> 01:39:10,182
I remember...

2148
01:39:10,417 --> 01:39:13,452
my exact balance as of yesterday.

2149
01:39:14,087 --> 01:39:15,988
- Let's save the speculation for later.
- Agreed.

2150
01:39:15,989 --> 01:39:17,856
The clock is ticking.

2151
01:39:17,857 --> 01:39:18,824
All right.

2152
01:39:18,992 --> 01:39:20,759
Okay, everyone.

2153
01:39:20,760 --> 01:39:23,696
So the first question could be...

2154
01:39:23,697 --> 01:39:25,264
"Who has the most prize money?"

2155
01:39:25,632 --> 01:39:26,565
What about this?

2156
01:39:26,833 --> 01:39:27,866
What's the highest balance?

2157
01:39:28,235 --> 01:39:29,635
(Current highest balance: 13,000 dollars)

2158
01:39:29,636 --> 01:39:31,904
- Top three is better.
- Wouldn't that give us more coverage?

2159
01:39:31,905 --> 01:39:33,940
- That's the safest bet.
- Since it captures first place anyway.

2160
01:39:34,374 --> 01:39:35,741
(Current second-highest balance:
12,000 dollars)

2161
01:39:35,742 --> 01:39:37,309
- All right, let's ask that.
- Be right back.

2162
01:39:37,310 --> 01:39:38,510
What if they reject that phrasing?

2163
01:39:38,511 --> 01:39:39,278
Rank order.

2164
01:39:39,413 --> 01:39:41,447
Then we rethink it.

2165
01:39:41,782 --> 01:39:42,815
Then we regroup.

2166
01:39:42,816 --> 01:39:43,849
- Got it.
- Back and forth we go.

2167
01:39:43,850 --> 01:39:44,783
Back and forth.

2168
01:39:45,118 --> 01:39:46,518
At the very least,
we need to know who's number one.

2169
01:39:46,519 --> 01:39:48,053
If we know who holds
the biggest balance...

2170
01:39:54,728 --> 01:39:57,530
(The Community Center)

2171
01:40:01,868 --> 01:40:04,136
This is the Reporter.
I'd like to request an information check.

2172
01:40:04,538 --> 01:40:06,839
The Reporter information inquiry
will now begin.

2173
01:40:09,342 --> 01:40:11,777
(As of now, who has...)

2174
01:40:16,416 --> 01:40:19,451
"Who are the top three
in cumulative prize money so far,"

2175
01:40:19,452 --> 01:40:21,520
"and what are their balances?"

2176
01:40:25,826 --> 01:40:29,896
The Reporter may only access one piece
of information per inquiry.

2177
01:40:31,264 --> 01:40:33,465
Currently,
who has the most cumulative prize money?

2178
01:40:35,769 --> 01:40:38,070
It might come back as me.

2179
01:40:38,572 --> 01:40:40,039
What makes you say that?

2180
01:40:40,040 --> 01:40:43,409
We discussed targeting Hippo together.

2181
01:40:43,410 --> 01:40:44,710
Can you vouch for me on that?

2182
01:40:44,711 --> 01:40:45,945
If not, I'm walking out.

2183
01:40:45,946 --> 01:40:47,480
Well, you're the one...

2184
01:40:47,714 --> 01:40:49,448
who walked away with her 8,000 dollars.

2185
01:40:49,449 --> 01:40:50,349
Right.

2186
01:40:50,350 --> 01:40:51,517
You took her money.

2187
01:40:52,880 --> 01:40:55,148
Currently,
who has the most cumulative prize money?

2188
01:40:56,123 --> 01:40:58,691
The resident
with the largest balance is...

2189
01:40:59,185 --> 01:41:00,296
Gray.

2190
01:41:00,296 --> 01:41:01,226
(The resident with the highest balance:
Gray)

2191
01:41:09,302 --> 01:41:11,503
Even if we find out who it is,
what do we do?

2192
01:41:11,605 --> 01:41:13,606
We can't attack them anyway.

2193
01:41:13,607 --> 01:41:16,275
- Exactly.
- Knowing who it is makes a difference,

2194
01:41:16,543 --> 01:41:18,511
since we don't know
what missions are coming next.

2195
01:41:20,780 --> 01:41:22,881
That's an interesting result.

2196
01:41:33,093 --> 01:41:35,728
Let me share the results of the inquiry.

2197
01:41:35,729 --> 01:41:36,729
- Okay.
- First off,

2198
01:41:37,030 --> 01:41:40,165
I asked who the top three are
in cumulative prize money so far...

2199
01:41:40,166 --> 01:41:41,900
and what their balances are.

2200
01:41:43,436 --> 01:41:46,872
They told me that I was asking
for more than one piece of information.

2201
01:41:49,543 --> 01:41:53,312
So I asked who currently holds
the highest cumulative prize money.

2202
01:41:55,248 --> 01:41:56,615
And they gave me the answer.

2203
01:41:57,450 --> 01:41:58,316
We got him.

2204
01:42:02,355 --> 01:42:03,221
It's Gray.

2205
01:42:21,508 --> 01:42:23,136
We had no idea you were sitting
on that much cash.

2206
01:42:26,079 --> 01:42:27,413
If I'd known,

2207
01:42:28,248 --> 01:42:30,482
I would've gone after Gray.
I already knew his code.

2208
01:42:38,225 --> 01:42:39,526
Let me ask you something first.

2209
01:42:39,527 --> 01:42:40,893
Who did you attack last night?

2210
01:42:42,229 --> 01:42:43,996
I'm the one who eliminated Hippo.

2211
01:42:44,164 --> 01:42:45,631
I see.

2212
01:42:48,268 --> 01:42:50,469
Did you attack me too?

2213
01:42:50,470 --> 01:42:52,171
- I didn't touch you.
- Why not?

2214
01:42:53,673 --> 01:42:55,173
To be honest,

2215
01:42:55,174 --> 01:42:57,342
I suspected Hippo was the spy.

2216
01:42:57,343 --> 01:42:59,945
She kept pointing fingers...

2217
01:42:59,946 --> 01:43:01,380
at me all day yesterday,

2218
01:43:01,581 --> 01:43:03,482
so I started feeling threatened.

2219
01:43:03,483 --> 01:43:05,183
When I heard...

2220
01:43:05,184 --> 01:43:07,653
one of us had to be evicted,

2221
01:43:08,321 --> 01:43:11,223
I wanted to test...

2222
01:43:11,224 --> 01:43:13,492
if someone was the spy.

2223
01:43:14,327 --> 01:43:17,763
If you're suspicious of me,
I have no defense.

2224
01:43:19,105 --> 01:43:20,031
I was so disappointed.

2225
01:43:20,299 --> 01:43:24,769
He claims it was self-defense,

2226
01:43:24,770 --> 01:43:26,805
but was that really what it was?

2227
01:43:26,806 --> 01:43:28,941
Did someone attack him? No.

2228
01:43:29,310 --> 01:43:32,778
Even if you call it
the "hypocrisy" Superman talked about,

2229
01:43:32,779 --> 01:43:35,214
we put so much effort
into not attacking one another.

2230
01:43:35,215 --> 01:43:37,216
It felt like everything
we'd built together...

2231
01:43:37,350 --> 01:43:40,352
just crumbled to pieces.

2232
01:43:41,354 --> 01:43:44,022
It came as a complete shock.

2233
01:43:44,524 --> 01:43:47,025
He was someone the whole house trusted,

2234
01:43:47,026 --> 01:43:49,194
the one who always played mediator.

2235
01:43:49,195 --> 01:43:52,831
I admit I suspected Hippo at first,

2236
01:43:52,832 --> 01:43:55,634
and I talked through
those suspicions with him.

2237
01:43:55,635 --> 01:43:58,137
But I never imagined
he would actually step up...

2238
01:43:58,138 --> 01:43:59,738
and take Hippo out.

2239
01:44:00,306 --> 01:44:03,108
I genuinely never saw that coming.

2240
01:44:03,109 --> 01:44:06,178
Yesterday,
I felt guilty just for doubting him,

2241
01:44:06,179 --> 01:44:08,647
so I gave him my favorability vote.

2242
01:44:09,115 --> 01:44:11,216
And it turns out he eliminated Hippo
entirely on his own.

2243
01:44:11,584 --> 01:44:15,487
I felt so betrayed, and that quickly
turned into anger and disappointment.

2244
01:44:15,989 --> 01:44:18,157
I was speechless.

2245
01:44:18,525 --> 01:44:20,726
We've been under immense pressure...

2246
01:44:20,727 --> 01:44:23,095
not to go rogue...

2247
01:44:23,096 --> 01:44:25,564
or make unilateral calls.

2248
01:44:25,565 --> 01:44:28,234
I understand the temptation,

2249
01:44:28,401 --> 01:44:31,270
but we had a mutual pact
not to attack each other.

2250
01:44:31,271 --> 01:44:33,906
I couldn't believe
he went through with it anyway.

2251
01:44:34,107 --> 01:44:35,074
The thing is,

2252
01:44:35,608 --> 01:44:38,944
I knew his code inside and out.

2253
01:44:38,945 --> 01:44:40,946
Now that I know he did it,

2254
01:44:40,947 --> 01:44:42,647
I couldn't stop thinking...

2255
01:44:42,648 --> 01:44:44,416
that his 14,000 dollars could
have been mine.

2256
01:44:44,417 --> 01:44:45,951
How much would I be holding right now
if I'd pulled the trigger?

2257
01:44:47,787 --> 01:44:49,921
When she walked in with those questions,

2258
01:44:49,922 --> 01:44:51,190
I was already bracing myself...

2259
01:44:51,191 --> 01:44:52,758
to be exposed.

2260
01:44:53,059 --> 01:44:57,763
In a way, there's so much pressure...

2261
01:44:57,764 --> 01:45:00,566
stifling our freedom in this community.

2262
01:45:00,567 --> 01:45:02,868
We agreed not to run ideological checks
on each other.

2263
01:45:02,869 --> 01:45:07,506
But I wonder if that restraint
is actually misguided.

2264
01:45:07,507 --> 01:45:10,275
Someone might want to check a code once...

2265
01:45:10,276 --> 01:45:12,678
or eliminate someone...

2266
01:45:12,679 --> 01:45:14,580
they genuinely believe is the spy.

2267
01:45:14,581 --> 01:45:16,748
We've grown so defensive...

2268
01:45:16,749 --> 01:45:18,917
that the second anyone steps
over that line,

2269
01:45:18,918 --> 01:45:22,448
we instantly brand them a villain.

2270
01:45:22,449 --> 01:45:23,722
I find that unfortunate.

2271
01:45:28,395 --> 01:45:29,363
I have a question.

2272
01:45:29,364 --> 01:45:32,698
In Round Two, someone attempted
an Ideology Check...

2273
01:45:32,699 --> 01:45:34,500
and failed.

2274
01:45:34,501 --> 01:45:36,001
That was me.

2275
01:45:36,770 --> 01:45:37,703
That was me.

2276
01:45:37,971 --> 01:45:39,305
So you attacked Hippo in Round Two...

2277
01:45:39,306 --> 01:45:40,339
and went after her again in Round Three?

2278
01:45:40,340 --> 01:45:42,741
That's right. I was planning to burn...

2279
01:45:43,610 --> 01:45:45,077
two attack tokens.

2280
01:45:45,678 --> 01:45:47,346
Look at it this way.

2281
01:45:47,347 --> 01:45:50,282
If Gray is telling the truth,

2282
01:45:50,784 --> 01:45:53,185
it makes it far less likely...

2283
01:45:53,186 --> 01:45:55,087
that he's the spy.

2284
01:45:55,088 --> 01:45:59,925
At the very least,
he isn't the one who attacked me.

2285
01:46:00,126 --> 01:46:01,960
Because the spy wouldn't have missed.

2286
01:46:01,961 --> 01:46:02,794
Exactly.

2287
01:46:03,196 --> 01:46:05,664
They bided their time until Round Three...

2288
01:46:05,665 --> 01:46:07,399
- One shot, one kill.
- and took me down in a single blow.

2289
01:46:09,335 --> 01:46:11,536
(The favorability vote)

2290
01:46:14,007 --> 01:46:15,875
I think we can safely rule out Gray...

2291
01:46:15,876 --> 01:46:17,876
as the spy.

2292
01:46:18,211 --> 01:46:20,279
You don't have to clear me completely.

2293
01:46:20,280 --> 01:46:21,580
To an extent, at least.

2294
01:46:21,998 --> 01:46:24,734
Yesterday, I was wondering...

2295
01:46:25,652 --> 01:46:28,153
how many attacks the spy actually gets.

2296
01:46:29,589 --> 01:46:31,490
We still have the favorability vote
to finish,

2297
01:46:31,491 --> 01:46:33,425
so we can table this for later.

2298
01:46:33,426 --> 01:46:34,560
We also only have 25 minutes left
to decide...

2299
01:46:34,561 --> 01:46:36,028
whether to use the immunity card.

2300
01:46:36,029 --> 01:46:36,895
Agreed.

2301
01:46:41,634 --> 01:46:43,168
Can I say something?

2302
01:46:44,370 --> 01:46:45,837
Just one thing.

2303
01:46:46,906 --> 01:46:48,640
Once the Reporter is evicted,

2304
01:46:48,641 --> 01:46:50,442
the role is gone for good.

2305
01:46:50,443 --> 01:46:52,143
There won't be a replacement.

2306
01:46:53,112 --> 01:46:55,447
I said that assuming...

2307
01:46:55,448 --> 01:46:57,315
the immunity card would be used on me.

2308
01:46:57,716 --> 01:46:59,451
Whether someone is a spy or a traitor,

2309
01:46:59,452 --> 01:47:01,920
in my eyes, it's the exact same thing.

2310
01:47:04,724 --> 01:47:05,824
First of all...

2311
01:47:06,092 --> 01:47:09,561
we need to accept that right now,

2312
01:47:09,562 --> 01:47:12,263
we have no mechanism to penalize anyone...

2313
01:47:12,264 --> 01:47:14,066
or even pinpoint who needs exposing.

2314
01:47:14,067 --> 01:47:15,534
And looking at the situation,

2315
01:47:15,535 --> 01:47:17,535
Nangja is the Reporter,

2316
01:47:17,536 --> 01:47:19,838
and she's currently on the chopping block.

2317
01:47:19,973 --> 01:47:21,407
It's vital to remember...

2318
01:47:21,408 --> 01:47:23,541
her role is entirely unique.

2319
01:47:23,542 --> 01:47:25,844
Nobody else can step into her shoes
once she's gone.

2320
01:47:26,045 --> 01:47:28,480
We still have plenty of time left,

2321
01:47:28,481 --> 01:47:32,217
which means there will be plenty
of moments where we need a Reporter.

2322
01:47:32,218 --> 01:47:33,284
That's just a reality.

2323
01:47:35,121 --> 01:47:37,456
What unsettled me...

2324
01:47:37,457 --> 01:47:39,658
was hearing people debate...

2325
01:47:39,659 --> 01:47:42,260
whether we'd even need a Reporter
moving forward...

2326
01:47:42,261 --> 01:47:45,464
just to justify using the immunity card.

2327
01:47:45,465 --> 01:47:47,165
It felt deeply uncomfortable...

2328
01:47:47,166 --> 01:47:50,168
and I didn't want any part
of that conversation.

2329
01:47:50,169 --> 01:47:52,270
It felt like people had changed so much,

2330
01:47:52,772 --> 01:47:55,874
and watching that happen was painful.

2331
01:47:56,175 --> 01:47:58,543
At the same time, maybe it was inevitable.

2332
01:47:58,778 --> 01:48:00,546
If this debate is going to drag on,

2333
01:48:00,547 --> 01:48:02,881
why don't we cast our votes while we talk?

2334
01:48:02,882 --> 01:48:04,550
Good idea. Time is running out.

2335
01:48:04,717 --> 01:48:07,319
Let's vote in the order we're seated.

2336
01:48:07,320 --> 01:48:08,186
Benjamin can go first.

2337
01:48:08,621 --> 01:48:12,324
This might be uncomfortable to bring up.

2338
01:48:12,692 --> 01:48:15,427
Nangja placed an embargo earlier,

2339
01:48:15,428 --> 01:48:17,496
so we have to factor that in...

2340
01:48:17,497 --> 01:48:20,198
when evaluating
whether she truly fulfilled her role...

2341
01:48:20,500 --> 01:48:22,734
as the Reporter.

2342
01:48:22,735 --> 01:48:24,770
Let me address that.

2343
01:48:24,771 --> 01:48:27,940
There was simply no more information
I could extract that day.

2344
01:48:27,941 --> 01:48:30,109
I worried that
if I came back empty-handed...

2345
01:48:30,110 --> 01:48:32,611
and announced we were out of inquiries,

2346
01:48:32,612 --> 01:48:36,148
suspicion would immediately
swing back to you.

2347
01:48:36,449 --> 01:48:38,417
It might sound absurd,

2348
01:48:38,418 --> 01:48:39,751
but I did it to protect you.

2349
01:48:39,752 --> 01:48:42,487
You claim you placed an embargo
for my sake,

2350
01:48:42,488 --> 01:48:45,323
yet the second I woke up,
you came straight to me...

2351
01:48:45,916 --> 01:48:47,359
and started probing.

2352
01:48:47,460 --> 01:48:51,029
- That seems a bit contradictory.
- I was deeply suspicious of you,

2353
01:48:51,030 --> 01:48:52,697
yet it broke my heart...

2354
01:48:52,698 --> 01:48:55,300
to think you might get targeted
without a shred of hard evidence.

2355
01:48:55,301 --> 01:48:57,335
What does that have to do
with the issue at hand?

2356
01:49:00,940 --> 01:49:03,108
Didn't she bring back
critical intel today?

2357
01:49:03,509 --> 01:49:04,476
She did.

2358
01:49:04,644 --> 01:49:06,778
In terms of the action itself,
isn't what he did far worse?

2359
01:49:07,847 --> 01:49:09,514
Isn't outright betrayal worse?

2360
01:49:15,588 --> 01:49:16,621
The Reporter did bring back...

2361
01:49:16,689 --> 01:49:20,358
crucial information today.

2362
01:49:21,561 --> 01:49:24,796
At the end of the day, it's Genie's call.

2363
01:49:24,797 --> 01:49:26,365
Everything rests on her.

2364
01:49:26,933 --> 01:49:28,367
I see what this is.

2365
01:49:29,335 --> 01:49:30,335
So...

2366
01:49:31,771 --> 01:49:33,972
I'm suspicious of Benjamin.

2367
01:49:34,274 --> 01:49:35,540
He turned aggressive out of nowhere.

2368
01:49:39,245 --> 01:49:41,012
(The favorability vote)

2369
01:49:41,013 --> 01:49:45,550
The Community Center closes
in ten minutes.

2370
01:49:53,226 --> 01:49:53,892
(Tell her.)

2371
01:49:55,261 --> 01:49:56,228
(Ask her for it.)

2372
01:49:58,730 --> 01:49:59,831
Is this what the pressure feels like?

2373
01:50:07,306 --> 01:50:10,508
We have to weigh the potential value...

2374
01:50:10,509 --> 01:50:12,110
of the single inquiry...

2375
01:50:12,478 --> 01:50:14,146
she gets tomorrow.

2376
01:50:14,313 --> 01:50:17,048
I can't force her to give up her immunity,

2377
01:50:17,316 --> 01:50:18,850
but one thing is certain.

2378
01:50:18,851 --> 01:50:21,066
If the Reporter is eliminated,
there's no replacing...

2379
01:50:21,067 --> 01:50:23,221
what that role provides for the community.

2380
01:50:23,322 --> 01:50:25,156
(Polar Bear pressuring her
to surrender her immunity.)

2381
01:50:25,157 --> 01:50:26,357
(Until the Community Center closes)

2382
01:50:26,358 --> 01:50:28,660
The immunity card belongs to Genie.

2383
01:50:28,661 --> 01:50:29,694
- Yes.
- Right.

2384
01:50:29,695 --> 01:50:30,695
And...

2385
01:50:30,830 --> 01:50:32,732
it's fair for the leader...

2386
01:50:32,733 --> 01:50:34,466
to share her thoughts...

2387
01:50:34,467 --> 01:50:35,801
on rescuing a candidate,

2388
01:50:36,301 --> 01:50:38,703
but whether she plays it or not...

2389
01:50:38,871 --> 01:50:41,239
- is entirely up to her.
- Exactly.

2390
01:50:41,240 --> 01:50:43,909
It's really not our place to tell her
what to do with it.

2391
01:50:43,910 --> 01:50:47,011
I'm not telling her what to do.

2392
01:50:47,012 --> 01:50:49,280
Let me hold onto it while I think.

2393
01:50:49,281 --> 01:50:52,320
I'm just giving her
perspectives to weigh...

2394
01:50:52,321 --> 01:50:55,153
before she makes her own choice.

2395
01:50:55,755 --> 01:50:56,755
I believe that's only fair.

2396
01:51:05,431 --> 01:51:07,332
The Community Center...

2397
01:51:07,667 --> 01:51:10,902
- closes in two minutes.
- She needs to decide right now.

2398
01:51:16,342 --> 01:51:17,943
(Until the Community Center closes)

2399
01:51:20,713 --> 01:51:22,047
It's your decision.

2400
01:51:22,581 --> 01:51:24,182
Thirty seconds left.

2401
01:51:25,451 --> 01:51:27,419
This is driving me crazy.

2402
01:51:29,155 --> 01:51:30,689
If you're going,
you need to run right now.

2403
01:51:30,690 --> 01:51:31,756
You have to make the call.

2404
01:51:33,659 --> 01:51:35,393
Nobody...

2405
01:51:35,394 --> 01:51:36,394
is forcing you.

2406
01:51:36,395 --> 01:51:37,829
We won't know the right answer...

2407
01:51:37,830 --> 01:51:39,197
until the game is completely over.

2408
01:51:40,566 --> 01:51:42,534
(Until the Community Center closes)

2409
01:51:46,506 --> 01:51:48,207
Wait. What do I do?

2410
01:51:48,908 --> 01:51:50,141
Wait, this is...

2411
01:51:56,682 --> 01:51:58,816
You have to choose. We're out of time.

2412
01:52:01,721 --> 01:52:03,689
(Until the Community Center closes)

2413
01:52:08,561 --> 01:52:09,461
Hold on.

2414
01:52:09,462 --> 01:52:11,329
Wait, the clock...

2415
01:52:11,831 --> 01:52:12,898
Come with me.

2416
01:52:12,899 --> 01:52:13,999
Whatever.

2417
01:52:21,941 --> 01:52:23,942
(Until the Community Center closes)

2418
01:52:26,612 --> 01:52:29,280
- Wait!
- The Community Center is now closed.

2419
01:52:34,720 --> 01:52:35,620
Am I too late?

2420
01:52:39,559 --> 01:52:40,359
Did I miss it?

2421
01:52:50,803 --> 01:52:53,204
The Community Center is closed,

2422
01:52:53,205 --> 01:52:56,341
so immunity transfers are
no longer permitted.

2423
01:52:57,577 --> 01:52:59,945
I'm not even a second late.

2424
01:53:01,514 --> 01:53:02,714
Is it really closed?

2425
01:53:03,482 --> 01:53:06,084
(Immunity transfers are
no longer permitted.)

2426
01:53:07,053 --> 01:53:08,153
Please.

2427
01:53:12,825 --> 01:53:14,659
Wait.

2428
01:53:15,261 --> 01:53:16,127
Come on.

2429
01:53:17,030 --> 01:53:17,929
I feel...

2430
01:53:18,431 --> 01:53:20,032
It's not your fault.

2431
01:53:21,200 --> 01:53:22,467
It's natural to hesitate.

2432
01:53:22,468 --> 01:53:24,102
I hesitated for too long.

2433
01:53:24,103 --> 01:53:25,336
- Oh, no.
- It's totally normal.

2434
01:53:25,705 --> 01:53:27,739
I should've just been a little faster.

2435
01:53:28,107 --> 01:53:30,041
- It's okay.
- I was too late.

2436
01:53:30,409 --> 01:53:31,976
Really, anyone would understand.

2437
01:53:32,111 --> 01:53:33,078
Anyone...

2438
01:53:33,847 --> 01:53:35,080
would have hesitated.

2439
01:53:35,414 --> 01:53:36,313
It's all right.

2440
01:53:37,083 --> 01:53:38,183
Hey, don't cry.

2441
01:53:38,184 --> 01:53:40,352
I'm so sorry.
I took too long to make up my mind.

2442
01:53:40,353 --> 01:53:41,753
I just...

2443
01:53:43,723 --> 01:53:45,724
It's okay. Don't cry.

2444
01:53:51,030 --> 01:53:54,666
If I'd only been a few seconds faster.

2445
01:53:54,667 --> 01:53:56,668
It's all right.
You did everything you could.

2446
01:54:06,212 --> 01:54:08,914
You sprinted all the way here to save me.

2447
01:54:09,850 --> 01:54:11,884
I feel so selfish.

2448
01:54:14,587 --> 01:54:16,221
You're not selfish at all.
It's only human.

2449
01:54:16,555 --> 01:54:17,388
Let's go.

2450
01:54:18,124 --> 01:54:20,892
Let's go, sweetie.

2451
01:54:21,360 --> 01:54:22,360
Let's go.

2452
01:54:23,529 --> 01:54:25,130
I'm so sorry.

2453
01:54:26,999 --> 01:54:28,900
Why are you crying?

2454
01:54:38,044 --> 01:54:39,144
(The announcement will now begin.)

2455
01:54:39,145 --> 01:54:41,680
Official activities for today
have concluded.

2456
01:54:42,748 --> 01:54:44,215
Today's evictee is...

2457
01:54:44,784 --> 01:54:47,619
Nangja.

2458
01:54:48,020 --> 01:54:50,989
Resident Nangja,

2459
01:54:51,757 --> 01:54:56,627
please leave the Community House
immediately.

2460
01:54:57,863 --> 01:54:59,730
We wish you a peaceful night.

2461
01:55:23,022 --> 01:55:25,323
Who starts running
with only ten seconds left?

2462
01:55:25,625 --> 01:55:28,026
Genie, if you wanted to hold onto it,

2463
01:55:28,027 --> 01:55:29,928
you should've just been honest.

2464
01:55:30,229 --> 01:55:32,097
Why make a dash when there were
only ten seconds on the clock?

2465
01:55:32,098 --> 01:55:34,032
You're not Usain Bolt.

2466
01:55:34,100 --> 01:55:35,501
Nobody covers that distance
in ten seconds.

2467
01:55:35,502 --> 01:55:38,303
Can we talk about the hypocrisy here?

2468
01:55:38,304 --> 01:55:40,238
Let's cut the drama.

2469
01:55:40,573 --> 01:55:41,640
She was putting on a performance.

2470
01:55:41,641 --> 01:55:44,209
Is she serious?
She knew the doors were closing.

2471
01:55:44,210 --> 01:55:45,544
"What should I do?"

2472
01:55:45,545 --> 01:55:47,512
You should've been running already.

2473
01:55:47,680 --> 01:55:49,047
It gave me chills.

2474
01:55:49,181 --> 01:55:51,048
And do you know what everyone was saying?

2475
01:55:51,550 --> 01:55:52,551
"Anyone would have hesitated."

2476
01:55:52,552 --> 01:55:54,319
"We would've done the same thing."

2477
01:55:54,320 --> 01:55:56,888
No, I wouldn't have.
I would've handed it over.

2478
01:55:57,156 --> 01:55:58,823
I really don't get that logic.

2479
01:55:59,025 --> 01:56:00,625
You know what all these people have
in common?

2480
01:56:00,626 --> 01:56:01,726
They're remarkably understanding...

2481
01:56:01,727 --> 01:56:04,329
because it's not their neck on the line.

2482
01:56:04,630 --> 01:56:07,565
Just like in the real world,
the people at the bottom take the hit,

2483
01:56:07,566 --> 01:56:09,901
while the ones at the top...

2484
01:56:09,902 --> 01:56:11,936
sympathize, shrug, and let it slide.

2485
01:56:12,238 --> 01:56:13,872
That's why someone
in my position has to do...

2486
01:56:13,873 --> 01:56:15,540
whatever it takes to scrape their way up.

2487
01:56:17,076 --> 01:56:18,443
I'm heartbroken...

2488
01:56:18,444 --> 01:56:20,979
that we lost the Reporter entirely.

2489
01:56:20,980 --> 01:56:22,881
Was allowing her eviction really
the right call?

2490
01:56:23,115 --> 01:56:26,017
What kind of blind spot does this leave us
with tomorrow?

2491
01:56:26,018 --> 01:56:27,952
Those doubts kept gnawing at me.

2492
01:56:28,154 --> 01:56:29,821
If she had just been an ordinary resident,

2493
01:56:29,822 --> 01:56:32,090
I probably would've pushed much harder.

2494
01:56:32,391 --> 01:56:33,758
I deliberately challenged...

2495
01:56:33,759 --> 01:56:35,259
whether her holding onto the immunity...

2496
01:56:35,260 --> 01:56:37,395
was truly justifiable,

2497
01:56:37,530 --> 01:56:39,631
trying to turn up the pressure.

2498
01:56:39,858 --> 01:56:42,626
As leader,
that was the most leverage I had.

2499
01:56:43,502 --> 01:56:45,837
I felt awful.

2500
01:56:45,838 --> 01:56:48,372
My only real ally got eliminated,
and it stung.

2501
01:56:48,674 --> 01:56:51,142
I desperately wanted to save her.

2502
01:56:51,544 --> 01:56:52,611
She stood by me through everything.

2503
01:56:52,645 --> 01:56:54,212
I just wish she knew
how deeply sorry I am.

2504
01:56:58,217 --> 01:57:01,619
In my head, the choice was already made.

2505
01:57:01,788 --> 01:57:04,322
I had already calculated...

2506
01:57:04,323 --> 01:57:07,994
that keeping the immunity card...

2507
01:57:07,995 --> 01:57:10,162
was the smarter play heading
into tomorrow.

2508
01:57:10,663 --> 01:57:13,932
Then my heart started fighting my head.

2509
01:57:13,933 --> 01:57:17,636
I had genuinely grown attached to her.

2510
01:57:17,970 --> 01:57:20,405
Watching someone walk out the door...

2511
01:57:20,406 --> 01:57:23,141
was unbearable.

2512
01:57:23,943 --> 01:57:24,909
Maybe...

2513
01:57:26,078 --> 01:57:28,813
I looked at it too clinically.

2514
01:57:28,981 --> 01:57:30,882
If I was going to feel this sick
about it afterward...

2515
01:57:31,350 --> 01:57:34,018
My head is spinning with so many emotions.

2516
01:57:35,154 --> 01:57:36,121
It's just...

2517
01:57:37,756 --> 01:57:38,789
I have such mixed emotions,

2518
01:57:40,059 --> 01:57:42,394
and they're in complete collision.

2519
01:57:52,104 --> 01:57:54,806
I feel relief, but also deep guilt.

2520
01:57:55,773 --> 01:57:59,042
It feels freeing,
yet it leaves such a bitter aftertaste.

2521
01:57:59,378 --> 01:58:02,413
This whole ordeal proved to me...

2522
01:58:02,438 --> 01:58:04,172
that the utopian society
they worked so hard to preach...

2523
01:58:04,417 --> 01:58:06,117
was fundamentally broken.

2524
01:58:06,952 --> 01:58:08,553
Gray was the one who eliminated a member,

2525
01:58:08,787 --> 01:58:11,356
yet nobody had the guts
to hold him accountable...

2526
01:58:11,357 --> 01:58:13,458
or even openly condemn him.

2527
01:58:13,459 --> 01:58:15,787
Because deep down, they knew
they might make the same move.

2528
01:58:15,962 --> 01:58:17,795
It was completely hypocritical.

2529
01:58:18,063 --> 01:58:21,399
It's just collective virtue signaling,

2530
01:58:21,534 --> 01:58:24,202
a mutual pact to conceal
their own self-interest.

2531
01:58:24,203 --> 01:58:26,204
It proved it to me once again.

2532
01:58:26,205 --> 01:58:29,174
It was a lovely fantasy, nothing more.

2533
01:58:29,375 --> 01:58:31,276
She promised she'd build a community...

2534
01:58:31,277 --> 01:58:34,779
where everyone could survive
together until the very end.

2535
01:58:34,780 --> 01:58:37,882
Yet when the stakes were real,
she couldn't even wield her influence.

2536
01:58:38,150 --> 01:58:39,817
It's textbook populism.

2537
01:58:40,152 --> 01:58:42,252
Feed people sweet platitudes...

2538
01:58:42,253 --> 01:58:44,655
just to win their loyalty.

2539
01:58:44,656 --> 01:58:46,157
Then take zero accountability
when things fall apart.

2540
01:58:46,325 --> 01:58:49,527
The person facing eviction was sitting
right beside her,

2541
01:58:49,695 --> 01:58:52,331
yet instead of genuine empathy,

2542
01:58:52,332 --> 01:58:54,299
she was only thinking about
what utility my role had left.

2543
01:58:54,300 --> 01:58:57,101
She couldn't even connect
with her own people.

2544
01:58:57,102 --> 01:58:59,104
It laid bare that all
those grand speeches...

2545
01:58:59,105 --> 01:59:00,438
were just empty words.

2546
01:59:00,439 --> 01:59:03,741
Even though I was eliminated,
I have no regrets.

2547
01:59:04,510 --> 01:59:06,044
I saw it coming.

2548
01:59:07,012 --> 01:59:09,914
I gained so much from this experience.

2549
01:59:10,249 --> 01:59:12,183
Above all, I realized just
how much growing I still have to do.

2550
01:59:12,184 --> 01:59:14,085
I have a long road ahead of me.

2551
01:59:14,086 --> 01:59:17,956
I want to understand people
through diverse lenses.

2552
01:59:18,358 --> 01:59:21,358
I want to take the complex personalities
I met here...

2553
01:59:22,161 --> 01:59:24,529
and breathe life into them
through my acting.

2554
01:59:27,766 --> 01:59:31,268
Today's evictee, Nangja,

2555
01:59:32,571 --> 01:59:35,072
was not the spy.

2556
01:59:44,383 --> 01:59:45,450
Is it really acceptable...

2557
01:59:46,585 --> 01:59:49,587
for residents to turn on each other
like this?

2558
01:59:50,489 --> 01:59:51,389
Me?

2559
01:59:51,390 --> 01:59:53,291
Why is everyone staying silent?

2560
01:59:57,463 --> 01:59:59,931
If my actions disrupted the group,
I apologize.

2561
01:59:59,932 --> 02:00:01,099
What I mean is...

2562
02:00:02,001 --> 02:00:04,135
It's a game,
so people understand the motive.

2563
02:00:04,270 --> 02:00:05,203
Still...

2564
02:00:05,471 --> 02:00:07,505
why did everyone make such a fuss before?

2565
02:00:08,274 --> 02:00:11,142
Tell me what you want me to do.

2566
02:00:11,143 --> 02:00:13,478
I'm just wondering
why the room suddenly went quiet.

2567
02:00:13,812 --> 02:00:15,346
- Right.
- I honestly don't get it.

2568
02:00:16,649 --> 02:00:18,883
I agree with Benjamin's point.

2569
02:00:18,884 --> 02:00:19,684
Yes.

2570
02:00:19,685 --> 02:00:21,753
Now that your actions are out in the open,

2571
02:00:21,754 --> 02:00:22,821
you have to take...

2572
02:00:22,822 --> 02:00:25,690
- I agree.
- the heat that comes with them.

2573
02:00:25,691 --> 02:00:27,525
Why don't we consider this?

2574
02:00:27,526 --> 02:00:30,530
It's clear that two people burned
attack tokens.

2575
02:00:30,531 --> 02:00:31,463
Right.

2576
02:00:31,464 --> 02:00:32,931
One is the spy,

2577
02:00:33,065 --> 02:00:36,067
and the other is someone
who violated our pact.

2578
02:00:36,068 --> 02:00:39,170
If we have a choice tomorrow,

2579
02:00:39,171 --> 02:00:43,441
we should agree
on which of the two to target.

2580
02:00:43,442 --> 02:00:44,375
- Agreed.
- I'm with you.

2581
02:00:44,376 --> 02:00:46,244
- What do you think? Not a bad plan.
- Makes sense.

2582
02:00:46,245 --> 02:00:47,678
If we have to target one,

2583
02:00:47,679 --> 02:00:50,448
shouldn't the spy be the priority?

2584
02:00:51,116 --> 02:00:53,150
I think the spy should go first too.

2585
02:00:53,151 --> 02:00:54,285
In my view...

2586
02:00:54,453 --> 02:00:55,486
What's the point?

2587
02:00:56,923 --> 02:00:58,656
Why are we so fixated on the spy?

2588
02:00:59,491 --> 02:01:00,791
Does anyone here actually know
their identity?

2589
02:01:00,792 --> 02:01:03,427
I got eliminated by the spy yesterday.

2590
02:01:03,428 --> 02:01:05,062
The spy took someone out.

2591
02:01:05,063 --> 02:01:07,832
So what do we actually gain
by taking out the spy?

2592
02:01:07,833 --> 02:01:09,667
Peace of mind, for one.

2593
02:01:11,036 --> 02:01:13,638
They've had me on edge since day one.

2594
02:01:13,805 --> 02:01:16,741
If taking someone out brings closure,

2595
02:01:16,742 --> 02:01:18,843
my vote goes to the spy.

2596
02:01:20,479 --> 02:01:22,613
Honestly,
I couldn't stand what I saw today.

2597
02:01:22,881 --> 02:01:24,715
Gray broke our agreement.

2598
02:01:24,817 --> 02:01:26,684
He worked on the campaign...

2599
02:01:26,685 --> 02:01:28,452
and pledged to protect the community
from the spy.

2600
02:01:28,453 --> 02:01:30,321
Then, right under our noses,
someone murdered one of our own.

2601
02:01:30,322 --> 02:01:33,624
And people are just sitting around
acting like their hands are tied.

2602
02:01:33,659 --> 02:01:35,193
It's infuriating.

2603
02:01:35,561 --> 02:01:37,061
I was furious...

2604
02:01:37,062 --> 02:01:38,830
the moment my ally was targeted.

2605
02:01:38,831 --> 02:01:40,064
What kind of logic is that?

2606
02:01:40,065 --> 02:01:43,668
Morally, what he did was worse
than what the spy did.

2607
02:01:43,669 --> 02:01:45,336
Yet everyone just sat there in silence.

2608
02:01:45,904 --> 02:01:47,605
That's why I had to speak up.

2609
02:01:47,606 --> 02:01:50,140
They made no effort to rescue
an innocent resident,

2610
02:01:50,141 --> 02:01:52,543
while the person who broke
our rules gets a free pass.

2611
02:01:52,544 --> 02:01:54,278
This community...

2612
02:01:54,279 --> 02:01:56,280
has lost its entire purpose.

2613
02:01:56,281 --> 02:01:57,548
It's already broken beyond repair.

2614
02:01:58,650 --> 02:02:00,317
Benjamin seemed furious.

2615
02:02:00,318 --> 02:02:02,219
Seriously, why is he that mad?

2616
02:02:02,621 --> 02:02:03,587
Tell me about it!

2617
02:02:03,588 --> 02:02:06,056
If you're going to eliminate me,
can you at least do it before noon?

2618
02:02:06,224 --> 02:02:07,558
I'm not eliminating you.

2619
02:02:08,026 --> 02:02:09,226
Because...

2620
02:02:09,227 --> 02:02:10,528
You're not the spy.

2621
02:02:10,529 --> 02:02:11,862
- That's true.
- Right.

2622
02:02:12,131 --> 02:02:13,699
- So...
- Because...

2623
02:02:13,700 --> 02:02:15,700
I have no reason to target you.

2624
02:02:15,701 --> 02:02:18,737
The way I see it, the spy...

2625
02:02:19,037 --> 02:02:20,371
must have an edge.

2626
02:02:20,372 --> 02:02:22,673
The person holding the second-highest
balance is definitely the spy.

2627
02:02:22,674 --> 02:02:23,741
- Absolutely.
- Right.

2628
02:02:28,447 --> 02:02:30,314
I'm still weighing my moves.

2629
02:02:30,315 --> 02:02:32,350
Nangja knew who the spy was.

2630
02:02:32,351 --> 02:02:34,419
"She got that intel directly
from the spy."

2631
02:02:34,420 --> 02:02:36,888
"The spy knows all the mechanics."

2632
02:02:36,889 --> 02:02:39,323
That means I could pull people
into my corner individually.

2633
02:02:39,425 --> 02:02:40,692
I could approach Genie...

2634
02:02:40,826 --> 02:02:42,193
and ask for her immunity card,

2635
02:02:42,194 --> 02:02:43,628
promising to carry her to the finals.

2636
02:02:43,629 --> 02:02:44,896
It could actually work.

2637
02:02:45,030 --> 02:02:47,298
With that in mind,
I'm playing cutthroat from here on out.

2638
02:02:47,433 --> 02:02:49,634
Because at the end of the day,
if I make it to the end,

2639
02:02:49,835 --> 02:02:52,036
I'm the one taking home the cash.

2640
02:02:53,939 --> 02:02:55,540
Hello. I'm Benjamin.

2641
02:02:56,909 --> 02:02:57,942
He's totally fluent.

2642
02:02:57,943 --> 02:02:59,010
He suddenly put on glasses.

2643
02:02:59,011 --> 02:03:00,845
I have an uncomfortable truth to share.

2644
02:03:00,846 --> 02:03:02,547
I don't have to speak English anymore.

2645
02:03:02,848 --> 02:03:04,048
The Benjamin Show is over.

2646
02:03:04,049 --> 02:03:05,283
I'm completely fluent in Korean.

2647
02:03:08,186 --> 02:03:10,521
You're all misreading this game.

2648
02:03:10,522 --> 02:03:13,224
This game doesn't end
just because you hunt down the spy.

2649
02:03:13,225 --> 02:03:15,893
And it doesn't end
just because the spy takes out...

2650
02:03:15,894 --> 02:03:16,928
a handful of you.

2651
02:03:18,597 --> 02:03:20,298
Don't delude yourselves...

2652
02:03:20,299 --> 02:03:23,267
into thinking you have any control
over this game.
